 Prompt: “Change each Motion slider and then replace the rotor recipe. Its purpose name must stay stable while current value text follows the actual setting. Preserve paused intent, focus and storage; do not infer assistive-technology qualification from modeled DOM assertions.”
 
+For [Motion focus after rotation](../../../authoring/motion-lab/README.md#keep-the-current-control-visible-after-rotation), keep resize visibility within the existing page-owned display lifecycle. Reveal only the current eligible foreground control against the viewport and active settings clip; include its label/value field when it fits. Cover the retained native case where document scrolling leaves the entire settings panel outside the viewport: do not veto native nearest scrolling merely because that intersection is empty. Never assign focus, change a range value, scroll an already visible field, resume the preview or queue future focus on return. Preserve newer focus and hidden, inert, disabled, background and terminal-departure guards. Use the actual-host RED/GREEN and full display/restoration files, with native rotation and focus-ring checks recorded separately from modeled rectangles.
+
 ## Backup-owned content feedback
 
 A complete-backup Import or Undo owns a journaled replacement, even when it temporarily shares the content-switch busy flag. Preserve cancellation generations, paused adoption and storage guards; announce a pending pack cancellation only for pack-owned work. A blur during held backup commit and successful adoption must not create a fictional newer-play-choice message on Home. Keep restoration feedback in Saves & loads and do not alter pager or profile ordering to fix this copy. See [backup feedback ownership](../../../docs/operation-focus.md#backup-feedback-ownership).
